[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":276},["ShallowReactive",2],{"news:\u002Fnews\u002F2023-08-13-moving-towards-a-more-aggressive-release-cycle":3,"news-timeline":57},{"id":4,"title":5,"author":6,"body":7,"date":47,"description":48,"extension":49,"meta":50,"navigation":51,"path":52,"readingTime":53,"seo":54,"stem":55,"__hash__":56},"news\u002Fnews\u002F2023-08-13-moving-towards-a-more-aggressive-release-cycle.md","Moving towards a more aggressive release cycle","dagbrown",{"type":8,"value":9,"toc":43},"minimark",[10,25,33,40],[11,12,13],"p",{},[14,15,19,20,24],"a",{"href":16,"rel":17},"https:\u002F\u002Fdownload.lunar-linux.org\u002Flunar\u002Fdaily\u002F",[18],"nofollow","Lunar Linux's new ",[21,22,23],"em",{},"daily"," releases.",[11,26,27,28,32],{},"One of the great things about Lunar Linux is that it's a rolling-release distro. Which is to say, once you've installed it, bringing it all up to date is a simple matter of using the ",[29,30,31],"code",{},"lunar update"," facility, which updates the moonbase--the software metadata repository--and then updates all of the software on your system to the current latest version. However, the latest official ISO release was a while ago. Which means that if you download Lunar Linux from the download page, you will have quite a long adventure ahead of you as everything needs to be updated.",[11,34,35,36,39],{},"That's why I've started making daily ISO releases. They started out as a way for me to incorporate new software into the Lunar Linux installer, then they turned into a way to test pull requests in the core moonbase, and now they're a reliable, safe, Lunar Linux installer. They work as USB media or if you burn them to a DVD--unfortunately they've grown too big for CD media over the years. If you want to install headless, they have serial-port installation support (think ",[29,37,38],{},"virsh console"," if you're wondering why anyone needs serial ports in 2023).",[11,41,42],{},"So if you want to try Lunar Linux, please try the daily ISO.",{"title":44,"searchDepth":45,"depth":45,"links":46},"",3,[],"2023-08-13","Daily ISO builds are now a reliable installer, so new installs start close to current.","md",{},true,"\u002Fnews\u002F2023-08-13-moving-towards-a-more-aggressive-release-cycle",2,{"title":5,"description":48},"news\u002F2023-08-13-moving-towards-a-more-aggressive-release-cycle","Reh81eJF1s6H1t2f6pFA7YEWkrCiVT2CucRL6hoZoJo",[58,59,63,67,71,75,79,83,87,91,95,99,102,106,110,114,118,121,125,129,133,137,141,145,149,153,157,161,165,169,173,177,181,185,189,193,197,201,205,209,213,217,221,225,229,233,237,241,245,249,253,257,261,265,268,272],{"title":5,"path":52,"date":47},{"title":60,"path":61,"date":62},"We are moving to libera.chat network","\u002Fnews\u002F2021-05-23-we-are-moving-to-libera-chat-network","2021-05-23",{"title":64,"path":65,"date":66},"We are still very much alive","\u002Fnews\u002F2017-10-18-we-are-still-very-much-alive","2017-10-18",{"title":68,"path":69,"date":70},"Lunar Linux 1.7.0 (i686 & x86_64) ISO’s released","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-10-11-lunar-linux-1-7-0-i686-and-x86-64-isos-released","2014-10-11",{"title":72,"path":73,"date":74},"Lunar Linux 1.7.0-rc2 (i686 & x86_64) ISO’s released","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-09-16-lunar-linux-1-7-0-rc2-i686-and-x86-64-isos-released","2014-09-16",{"title":76,"path":77,"date":78},"Service transition","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-05-24-service-transition","2014-05-24",{"title":80,"path":81,"date":82},"Services from lunar-linux.org may be disrupted","\u002Fnews\u002F2014-05-19-services-from-lunar-linux-org-may-be-disrupted","2014-05-19",{"title":84,"path":85,"date":86},"New installation ISO development","\u002Fnews\u002F2013-09-19-new-installation-iso-development","2013-09-19",{"title":88,"path":89,"date":90},"Moonbase Workflow","\u002Fnews\u002F2012-06-03-moonbase-workflow","2012-06-03",{"title":92,"path":93,"date":94},"new 32bit chroot image","\u002Fnews\u002F2012-04-01-new-32bit-chroot-image","2012-04-01",{"title":96,"path":97,"date":98},"Fut